module

public import StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.FlatCriterion
public import StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.FlatEquivalence

/-!
# Flatness and the relation subpresheaf of a sheaf of modules

Let `(C, O)` be a ringed site and let `F` be a sheaf of `O`-modules. Stacks 08FC characterises
flatness of `F` by a local factorisation property of the relations among its sections, and the
implication **(1) implies (2)** — flatness gives the criterion — is proved in
`StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.FlatCriterion` at `max v w` and in
`StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.FlatEquivalence` at a free section universe.

This file supplies the two ingredients that implication is assembled from, in the forms its
consumers use:

* the relation element `∑ᵢ (generator attached to aᵢ) ⊗ sᵢ` of `relSubmodule a ⊗ G`, which is
  where the relation `∑ᵢ aᵢ • sᵢ = 0` is consumed, together with its restrictions; and
* flatness read as a statement about a *locally* injective morphism of presheaves of modules,
  up to the element form `exists_covering_restrict_eq_zero_of_isFlat` in which it is applied.

## The argument

The source works with the sheaf of ideals `I ⊆ O_U` generated by `a₁, …, a_n` on the localised
site `C/U`; it observes that `∑ aⱼ ⊗ sⱼ` is a section of `I ⊗ F|_U` which dies in `F|_U`, that
flatness makes `I ⊗ F|_U → F|_U` injective, and then unwinds the algebraic equational criterion
over a covering on which the section already dies at the level of the presheaf tensor product.

Here localisation is replaced by the extension by zero `j_! I`, realised as the subpresheaf
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.relSubmodule` of the free presheaf of `O`-modules on `Hom(-, U)`; that is
the construction of `StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.FlatEquivalence`, which also
supplies the algebraic step `Stacks.SheafOfModules.exists_relFactorization`. What remains, and is
what this file does, is to turn flatness into local injectivity of the inclusion of the relation
subpresheaf tensored with `F`. That is done in three steps.

* A morphism of presheaves of modules which is locally injective stays locally injective after
  sheafification, so its sheafification is a monomorphism
  (`Stacks.SheafOfModules.mono_shf_map_of_isLocallyInjective`, of
  `StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.FlatEquivalenceConverse`). The inclusion of a
  subpresheaf is injective on sections, so this applies to it.
* Flatness is exactness of the tensor functor on *sheaves* of modules, so it makes the
  sheafification of the tensored morphism a monomorphism — but only for the *sheafified*
  morphism. Passing back to the presheaf-level one uses that sheafification does not see a local
  bijection in a tensor factor (`Stacks.isIso_sheafification_map_tensorRight_map`), applied to
  the two units of the sheafification adjunction. This is
  `Stacks.SheafOfModules.mono_shf_map_tensorRight_map_of_isFlat`.
* A morphism of presheaves of modules whose sheafification is a monomorphism is locally injective
  (`Stacks.SheafOfModules.isLocallyInjective_of_mono_shf_map`), which is the form the conclusion
  is consumed in: the relation element dies over `U`, hence dies on a covering of `U`. That
  composite is
  `Stacks.SheafOfModules.isLocallyInjective_tensorRight_map_of_isFlat` of `FlatCriterion`.

## Main results

* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.mono_shf_map_tensorRight_map_of_isFlat`: tensoring a locally injective
  morphism of presheaves of modules with a flat sheaf of modules and sheafifying gives a
  monomorphism.
* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.exists_covering_restrict_eq_zero_of_isFlat`: the element form of
  `Stacks.SheafOfModules.isLocallyInjective_tensorRight_map_of_isFlat` — a section of `P ⊗ F`
  killed in `Q ⊗ F` dies on a covering.
* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.tensorObj_map_relGen_tmul`: the restriction along `f : V ⟶ U` of the
  relation element of `relSubmodule a ⊗ G` over `U` is the relation element supported in the
  component indexed by `f`. That the element itself dies in `freeOn O U ⊗ G` is
  `Stacks.SheafOfModules.tensorRight_map_ι_app_eq_zero`, in
  `StacksFrontier/Algebra/Category/ModuleCat/Sheaf/FlatEquivalence.lean`.
* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.mono_of_isLocallyInjective_val`: a morphism of sheaves of modules whose
  underlying morphism of presheaves is locally injective is a monomorphism.

## Implementation notes

The universe of the sections of the structure sheaf is `max v w` rather than an independent `w`,
as in `StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.FlatEquivalence`, and for the same reason:
the free presheaf used to build the relation subpresheaf is free on the index set `V ⟶ U`, which
lives in the morphism universe.

The underlying presheaf of rings is spelled `Stacks.ringPresheaf O.obj` by the relation
subpresheaf and the algebraic step, and `(Stacks.commRingSheafToRingSheaf O).obj` by
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.shf` and the flatness material. The two are equal by `rfl`, but only
through an unfolding of `CategoryTheory.sheafCompose`, which is past the transparency at which
instances are synthesized and at which `rw` and `rfl` work. Two consequences are visible below.

* The section on the relation element keeps entirely to the first spelling and the section on
  flatness entirely to the second; the crossing happens once, where the second is applied to the
  inclusion of the relation subpresheaf.
* In the flatness section that unfolding is made available below default transparency by
  `attribute [local implicit_reducible] CategoryTheory.sheafCompose`. Without it the unavoidable
  mixed terms — `Stacks.SheafOfModules.shf` is stated in one spelling and `Stacks.tensorRight`
  in the other — cost more than the heartbeat budget of a declaration.

The local injectivity hypotheses are explicit arguments rather than instances, so that they can
be discharged across the two spellings by `exact`, which checks definitional equality at default
transparency.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 08FC](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/08FC)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 03ER](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03ER)
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory Opposite

universe w v u

namespace Stacks.SheafOfModules

section Mono

variable {C : Type u} [Category.{v} C] {J : GrothendieckTopology C}

/-- A morphism of sheaves of modules which is locally injective on the underlying presheaves is
a monomorphism: the underlying presheaves are sheaves, so locally injective means injective on
sections, and the functor to sheaves of abelian groups is faithful. -/
lemma mono_of_isLocallyInjective_val {R : Sheaf J RingCat.{max v w}}
    {M N : _root_.SheafOfModules.{max v w} R} (u : M ⟶ N)
    (h : Presheaf.IsLocallyInjective J ((PresheafOfModules.toPresheaf R.obj).map u.val)) :
    Mono u :=
  have : Sheaf.IsLocallyInjective ((_root_.SheafOfModules.toSheaf R).map u) := h
  (_root_.SheafOfModules.toSheaf R).mono_of_mono_map (Sheaf.mono_of_isLocallyInjective _)

end Mono

section Relation

variable {C : Type u} [Category.{v} C] {J : GrothendieckTopology C}
  {O : Sheaf J CommRingCat.{max v w}} {U : C} {n : ℕ}
  (a : Fin n → (ringPresheaf O.obj).obj (op U))
  {G : PresheafOfModules.{max v w} (ringPresheaf O.obj)}

/-- Restricting the relation element along `f : V ⟶ U` gives the relation element attached to the
restrictions, now supported in the component indexed by `f` rather than by the identity. -/
lemma tensorObj_map_relGen_tmul (s : Fin n → G.obj (op U)) {V : C} (f : V ⟶ U) (i : Fin n) :
    (tensorObj ((relSubmodule a).toPresheafOfModules) G).map f.op
        ((⟨relGen a (op U) (𝟙 U) i, relGen_mem a (op U) (𝟙 U) i⟩ :
          ((relSubmodule a).toPresheafOfModules).obj (op U))
            ⊗ₜ[(ringPresheaf O.obj).obj (op U)] s i)
      = (⟨relGen a (op V) f i, relGen_mem a (op V) f i⟩ :
          ((relSubmodule a).toPresheafOfModules).obj (op V))
        ⊗ₜ[(ringPresheaf O.obj).obj (op V)] G.map f.op (s i) := by
  refine Eq.trans (show (tensorObj ((relSubmodule a).toPresheafOfModules) G).map f.op
      ((⟨relGen a (op U) (𝟙 U) i, relGen_mem a (op U) (𝟙 U) i⟩ :
        ((relSubmodule a).toPresheafOfModules).obj (op U))
          ⊗ₜ[(ringPresheaf O.obj).obj (op U)] s i)
    = ((relSubmodule a).toPresheafOfModules).map f.op
        (⟨relGen a (op U) (𝟙 U) i, relGen_mem a (op U) (𝟙 U) i⟩ :
          ((relSubmodule a).toPresheafOfModules).obj (op U))
      ⊗ₜ[(ringPresheaf O.obj).obj (op V)] G.map f.op (s i) from rfl) ?_
  refine congrArg (fun y ↦ y ⊗ₜ[(ringPresheaf O.obj).obj (op V)] G.map f.op (s i))
    (Subtype.ext ?_)
  show (freeOn O U).map f.op (relGen a (op U) (𝟙 U) i) = relGen a (op V) f i
  exact (freeOn_map_relGen a f.op (𝟙 U) i).trans
    (congrArg (fun g ↦ relGen a (op V) g i) (Category.comp_id f))

end Relation

section Flat

-- The underlying presheaf of rings of `Stacks.commRingSheafToRingSheaf O` is
-- `Stacks.ringPresheaf O.obj`, but only after unfolding `CategoryTheory.sheafCompose`; making
-- that unfolding available below default transparency is what keeps the mixed terms of this
-- section within the heartbeat budget. See the implementation notes.
attribute [local implicit_reducible] CategoryTheory.sheafCompose

variable {C : Type u} [Category.{v} C] {J : GrothendieckTopology C}
  [J.HasSheafCompose (forget₂ CommRingCat.{max v w} RingCat.{max v w})]
  [J.WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{max v w}]
  [HasSheafify J AddCommGrpCat.{max v w}]
  {O : Sheaf J CommRingCat.{max v w}}

/-- Sheafification preserves local injectivity: the unit of the sheafification adjunction is
locally bijective, so a locally injective morphism factors through it as a locally injective
morphism. -/
lemma isLocallyInjective_shfRight_shf_map
    {P Q : PresheafOfModules.{max v w} (commRingSheafToRingSheaf O).obj} (u : P ⟶ Q)
    (hu : Presheaf.IsLocallyInjective J ((PresheafOfModules.toPresheaf _).map u)) :
    Presheaf.IsLocallyInjective J
      ((PresheafOfModules.toPresheaf _).map ((shfRight O).map ((shf O).map u))) := by
  have := hu
  have fac : (PresheafOfModules.toPresheaf (commRingSheafToRingSheaf O).obj).map
        ((shfAdj O).unit.app P) ≫
      (PresheafOfModules.toPresheaf (commRingSheafToRingSheaf O).obj).map
        ((shfRight O).map ((shf O).map u))
      = (PresheafOfModules.toPresheaf (commRingSheafToRingSheaf O).obj).map u ≫
        (PresheafOfModules.toPresheaf (commRingSheafToRingSheaf O).obj).map
          ((shfAdj O).unit.app Q) := by
    rw (transparency := .default) [← Functor.map_comp, ← Functor.map_comp,
      ← shfAdj_unit_naturality u]
  exact Presheaf.isLocallyInjective_of_isLocallyInjective_of_isLocallySurjective_fac J _ fac

/-- Sheafifying the tensor product with `F` of a unit of the sheafification adjunction is an
isomorphism: the unit is locally bijective, and sheafification does not see a local bijection in
a tensor factor. -/
lemma isIso_shf_map_tensorRight_map_unit
    (P : PresheafOfModules.{max v w} (commRingSheafToRingSheaf O).obj)
    (F : _root_.SheafOfModules.{max v w} (commRingSheafToRingSheaf O)) :
    IsIso ((shf O).map ((tensorRightOf O F).map ((shfAdj O).unit.app P))) :=
  Stacks.isIso_sheafification_map_tensorRight_map
    (show ringPresheaf O.obj ⟶ (commRingSheafToRingSheaf O).obj from
      𝟙 (commRingSheafToRingSheaf O).obj) ((shfAdj O).unit.app P)

/-- **Flatness, in the form the definition gives it.** Tensoring the *sheafification* of a
locally injective morphism of presheaves of modules by a flat sheaf of modules and sheafifying
gives a monomorphism. -/
lemma mono_shf_map_tensorRight_map_shfRight_map
    {P Q : PresheafOfModules.{max v w} (commRingSheafToRingSheaf O).obj} (u : P ⟶ Q)
    (hu : Presheaf.IsLocallyInjective J ((PresheafOfModules.toPresheaf _).map u))
    (F : _root_.SheafOfModules.{max v w} (commRingSheafToRingSheaf O)) (hF : IsFlat F) :
    Mono ((shf O).map ((tensorRightOf O F).map ((shfRight O).map ((shf O).map u)))) := by
  have := hu
  have := mono_shf_map_of_isLocallyInjective (R := commRingSheafToRingSheaf O) u
  rw [shfRight_map_eq]
  exact mono_shf_map_tensorRightOf_map_val hF ((shf O).map u)

/-- Tensoring with `F` and sheafifying is a functor, read on a composite. -/
private lemma shf_map_tensorRight_map_comp
    {P Q R : PresheafOfModules.{max v w} (commRingSheafToRingSheaf O).obj} (u : P ⟶ Q) (t : Q ⟶ R)
    (F : _root_.SheafOfModules.{max v w} (commRingSheafToRingSheaf O)) :
    (shf O).map ((tensorRightOf O F).map (u ≫ t))
      = (shf O).map ((tensorRightOf O F).map u) ≫ (shf O).map ((tensorRightOf O F).map t) := by
  rw [(tensorRightOf O F).map_comp]
  exact (shf O).map_comp _ _

/-- The diagonal of the unit square of the sheafification adjunction, tensored with a flat `F`
and sheafified, is a monomorphism: taken the other way round the square it is an isomorphism
followed by the monomorphism that flatness provides. -/
private lemma mono_shf_map_tensorRight_map_unit_comp
    {P Q : PresheafOfModules.{max v w} (commRingSheafToRingSheaf O).obj} (u : P ⟶ Q)
    (hu : Presheaf.IsLocallyInjective J ((PresheafOfModules.toPresheaf _).map u))
    (F : _root_.SheafOfModules.{max v w} (commRingSheafToRingSheaf O)) (hF : IsFlat F) :
    Mono ((shf O).map ((tensorRightOf O F).map (u ≫ (shfAdj O).unit.app Q))) := by
  rw [shfAdj_unit_naturality u, shf_map_tensorRight_map_comp]
  have := isIso_shf_map_tensorRight_map_unit P F
  have := mono_shf_map_tensorRight_map_shfRight_map u hu F hF
  exact mono_comp _ _

/-- **Flatness in the form in which it is used.** If `F` is a flat sheaf of `O`-modules and `u`
is a locally injective morphism of presheaves of `O`-modules, then the sheafification of `u ⊗ F`
is a monomorphism.

Flatness only applies to the *sheafification* of `u`; the two are compared by the square of the
unit of the sheafification adjunction, whose horizontal images under `(- ⊗ F)^#` are
isomorphisms. The diagonal of that square is therefore a monomorphism, and `u ⊗ F` is a factor of
it. -/
lemma mono_shf_map_tensorRight_map_of_isFlat
    {P Q : PresheafOfModules.{max v w} (commRingSheafToRingSheaf O).obj} (u : P ⟶ Q)
    (hu : Presheaf.IsLocallyInjective J ((PresheafOfModules.toPresheaf _).map u))
    (F : _root_.SheafOfModules.{max v w} (commRingSheafToRingSheaf O)) (hF : IsFlat F) :
    Mono ((shf O).map ((tensorRightOf O F).map u)) :=
  have := mono_shf_map_tensorRight_map_unit_comp u hu F hF
  mono_of_mono_fac (shf_map_tensorRight_map_comp u ((shfAdj O).unit.app Q) F).symm

/-- `Stacks.SheafOfModules.isLocallyInjective_tensorRight_map_of_isFlat` read on elements: a
section of `P ⊗ F` over `X` which dies in `Q ⊗ F` dies on a covering of `X`. This is the form in
which flatness is consumed. -/
lemma exists_covering_restrict_eq_zero_of_isFlat
    {P Q : PresheafOfModules.{max v w} (commRingSheafToRingSheaf O).obj} (u : P ⟶ Q)
    (hu : Presheaf.IsLocallyInjective J ((PresheafOfModules.toPresheaf _).map u))
    (F : _root_.SheafOfModules.{max v w} (commRingSheafToRingSheaf O)) (hF : IsFlat F)
    {X : Cᵒᵖ} (x : ((tensorRightOf O F).obj P).obj X)
    (hx : ((tensorRightOf O F).map u).app X x = 0) :
    ∃ S : Sieve X.unop, S ∈ J X.unop ∧
      ∀ ⦃V : C⦄ (f : V ⟶ X.unop), S f → ((tensorRightOf O F).obj P).map f.op x = 0 := by
  have hLI := isLocallyInjective_tensorRight_map_of_isFlat hF u hu
  have hx' : ((PresheafOfModules.toPresheaf (ringPresheaf O.obj)).map
        ((tensorRightOf O F).map u)).app X x
      = ((PresheafOfModules.toPresheaf (ringPresheaf O.obj)).map
        ((tensorRightOf O F).map u)).app X 0 := by
    rw [map_zero]
    exact hx
  refine ⟨_, Presheaf.equalizerSieve_mem J ((PresheafOfModules.toPresheaf
    (ringPresheaf O.obj)).map ((tensorRightOf O F).map u)) x 0 hx', fun {V} f hf ↦ ?_⟩
  exact (show ((tensorRightOf O F).obj P).map f.op x
    = ((tensorRightOf O F).obj P).map f.op 0 from hf).trans (map_zero _)

end Flat

end Stacks.SheafOfModules
